<article class="env-lemma" id="0H7L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H7L">Lemma <span data-tag="0H7L">10.30.8</span>.</a> Let $A \subset B$ be an inclusion of domains inducing an algebraic extension of fraction fields. If $J \subset B$ is a nonzero ideal, then $A \cap J$ is nonzero too. Thus the image of a proper closed subset of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B)$ is not dense in $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $x \in J$ be a nonzero element. Since $x$ is algebraic over the fraction field of $A$, there exists a $d \geq 1$ and $a_0, \ldots , a_ d \in A$ with $a_0, a_ d \not= 0$ such that $a_ d x^ d + a_{d - 1} x^{d - 1} + \ldots + a_0 = 0$ in $B$. Then $a_0 \in A \cap J$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>